      "path": "../experiments/runs/official_sonnet-5/baseline/WebTestBench_0023/rep1/result.md",
      "content": "# Test Result\n\n## Functionality\n- [X] FT-01: Sellers can create a listing by attaching one or more of their own product photos and supplying a title, description, non-negative price, category, condition, location, and upcycled status; the created listing retains and displays the submitted information.\n\n- [ ] FT-02: Sellers can edit the title, description, photos, price, category, condition, location, and upcycled status of an existing listing they own, and the saved listing displays the changes.\n  - Bug Report:\n    - Issue: No edit functionality exists for listings\n    - Actual: On My Listings, each owned listing only offers \"View\", \"Mark Sold\", and \"Delete\" actions — no Edit button. The product detail page for an owned listing (/product/prod-1) also has no edit control (checked all buttons/links via DOM query, none relate to editing). There is no way to change title, description, photos, price, category, condition, location, or upcycled status of an existing listing.\n\n- [X] FT-03: Sellers can mark an owned listing as sold or available and can delete it after confirmation; their listing view immediately reflects the resulting status or removal.\n\n- [X] FT-04: A listing marked sold or deleted is no longer offered to buyers in browse results and cannot be newly added to a cart or used to start a purchase request.\n\n- [X] FT-05: A user can register with a name, unique valid email address, password of at least six characters, and location; successful registration is confirmed and leaves the new user signed in.\n\n- [ ] FT-06: Buyers can combine category, minimum and maximum price, condition, distance, and upcycled-only filters and sort the available listings by newest, price, or distance; every result satisfies all active criteria.\n  - Bug Report:\n    - Issue: No true minimum price control; only a single price-cap slider exists\n    - Actual: The 'Price Range' filter renders only one slider thumb (aria-label 'Minimum', range 0-500) that actually functions as a maximum price cap: moving it from 0 lowered the displayed range to '$0 - $200' and excluded the $320 item while keeping the $175 item, i.e. it excludes items ABOVE the value, not below. There is no second thumb or input to set an actual price floor above $0, so buyers cannot filter out cheap items or combine a true minimum with a maximum. Category (Furniture -> 3 items), Condition (+New -> 2 items), Upcycled-only (5 items, all badged Upcycled), Max Distance (draggable, updates to e.g. '48 miles'), and Sort (Price: Low to High correctly ordered $45/$125/$175/$285/$320 within the upcycled filter) all worked correctly and combined together, but the missing minimum-price capability violates the requirement to filter by both minimum and maximum price.\n\n- [X] FT-07: Buyers can search available listings case-insensitively by words in the title, description, or location; every result matches the query, and clearing it restores the unsearched result set.\n\n- [X] FT-08: A signed-in buyer can add an available listing they do not own to the cart; the item is retained once with its title, photo, location, and price, and the cart total is correct.\n\n- [X] FT-09: A signed-in buyer can submit a non-empty purchase-request message for an available listing they do not own and receives visible confirmation that it was submitted.\n\n- [ ] FT-10: Choosing a category from the category-browsing page opens browse results containing only available listings in that category and shows a matching result count.\n  - Bug Report:\n    - Issue: Category browse link does not filter results\n    - Actual: On /categories page, 'Furniture' card shows '3 items'. Clicking it navigates to /?category=furniture, but the resulting Browse page shows all 10 listings (heading 'Browse All Items', 'paragraph: 10 items available') across all categories (Furniture, Clothing, Electronics, Home Decor, Books, Sports, Toys all represented), and the 'Furniture' checkbox in the sidebar filters remains unchecked. The category query param is not applied as a filter, so the result set and count do not match the 3-item Furniture count shown on the categories page.\n\n- [ ] FT-11: After a buyer submits a purchase request, the relevant seller can view the requested item and buyer message, and a cart request is reported as sent only after a request has been recorded for each cart item.\n  - Bug Report:\n    - Issue: No seller-facing view exists for buyer messages or purchase requests\n    - Actual: As buyer 'QA Buyer', sent a message to seller Emma Green via the Message Seller dialog on Mid-Century Modern Armchair (prod-1), and separately (as Emma Green) added 2 items from other sellers (James Wilson's Reclaimed Wood Bookshelf, Marcus Chen's Vintage Denim Jacket) to cart and clicked 'Send Purchase Request', which showed toast 'Purchase requests sent to sellers!' and cleared the cart. However, after logging in as the relevant sellers (Emma Green, and separately Marcus Chen), there is no way anywhere in the app to view received messages or purchase requests: the header has no messages/notifications icon (only search, Sell, cart, and avatar/menu icons - confirmed via DOM inspection: svg classes are lucide-search, lucide-plus, lucide-shopping-cart, avatar img, lucide-menu), the account dropdown only offers 'My Profile' (which 404s) and 'My Listings', and viewing the specific product detail page as its owner (Marcus Chen viewing prod-2, Emma Green viewing prod-1) shows no request/message content, count, or indicator at all - just the normal listing details plus a 'Manage Your Listings' button. Since sellers cannot view the requested item or buyer message anywhere, the first part of this requirement fails. The 'reported as sent only after recorded' behavior (toast appears immediately after clicking Send Purchase Request, cart clears) is present, but is unverifiable as being tied to actual per-item request recording given no seller-side visibility exists to confirm receipt.\n\n\n## Constraint\n- [X] CS-01: A login attempt using an email that is not registered is rejected and does not create an authenticated session.\n\n- [ ] CS-02: Registration rejects an email already used by an account, including a case-only variation, without replacing the existing account.\n  - Bug Report:\n    - Issue: Duplicate email not rejected on registration\n    - Actual: Registering with a case-only variation (TimQA.Tester@example.com) of an already-registered email (timqa.tester@example.com) succeeded and created a new account \"Tim Duplicate\" with toast \"Account created successfully!\". A subsequent registration using the exact same email (timqa.tester@example.com) also succeeded, creating another account \"Tim Exact Dup\". No duplicate-account rejection occurred in either case.\n\n- [ ] CS-03: A registered account can be authenticated only with its correct password; an incorrect password is rejected without creating a signed-in session.\n  - Bug Report:\n    - Issue: Password verification is not enforced correctly\n    - Actual: Logging into the newly registered account (timqa.tester@example.com) with its correct password (password1) was rejected with \"Invalid credentials\", so the registered account cannot be authenticated at all. Conversely, logging into a demo account (emma@example.com) succeeded using an arbitrary incorrect password (\"anything123\"); the login screen itself states \"(any password works)\" for demo accounts. Password is not verified against the account's actual password in either case.\n\n- [X] CS-04: Seller-management actions are available only for listings owned by the signed-in seller and are not exposed when that user views another seller's listing.\n\n- [X] CS-05: A listing cannot be created without at least one photo, a title, description, valid price, category, condition, and location, and the missing required information is identified to the seller.\n\n- [X] CS-06: A listing price must be a finite number greater than or equal to zero; negative or non-numeric prices are rejected without creating the listing.\n\n- [ ] CS-07: Creating or managing listings, adding items to or viewing the cart, and submitting purchase requests require a signed-in account; unauthenticated attempts are blocked with a clear sign-in prompt or redirect.\n  - Bug Report:\n    - Issue: Inconsistent auth guard: protected routes render blank page on direct navigation instead of sign-in prompt/redirect\n    - Actual: Authenticated-action guards work correctly when triggered via in-app buttons: clicking 'Add to Cart' while logged out redirects to /login with toast 'Please log in to add items to your cart'; clicking 'Message Seller' while logged out opens the message dialog but shows a disabled 'Log in to message' button instead of 'Send' (clear sign-in prompt). However, direct navigation to protected routes /cart and /create-listing while unauthenticated does NOT redirect to /login or show any sign-in prompt - both render a completely blank page (only the notification region, no header/banner, no content, no error message). This is inconsistent route-level protection: action-triggered guards are fine, but route-level guards for /cart and /create-listing are missing/broken, violating the requirement that unauthenticated attempts be 'blocked with a clear sign-in prompt or redirect' in all cases.\n\n\n## Interaction\n- [ ] IX-01: Attempting to register an existing email produces immediate, visible duplicate-account feedback and keeps the registration form available for correction.\n  - Bug Report:\n    - Issue: No duplicate-account feedback shown; form not kept for correction because registration succeeds instead\n    - Actual: Attempting to register with an already-used email (exact and case-variant) did not produce any duplicate warning; instead the app displayed \"Account created successfully!\" and navigated away from the registration form, signing in as a new duplicate account.\n\n- [X] IX-02: Search results and the available-item count update as the buyer types or clears a query, without requiring a separate search submission.\n\n- [X] IX-03: Changing any available filter or sort choice immediately updates the displayed listings and result count, and clearing all filters restores the unfiltered available listings.\n\n- [X] IX-04: Adding a listing to the cart produces immediate visible confirmation and updates the cart count, line item, and total without a manual reload.\n\n\n## Content\n- [X] CT-01: Each listing's details present its photos, title, description, price, category, condition, location, seller, listing date, availability, and upcycled status consistently with the listing data."
    }
  }
}
